scope one keystone in mantra -- the store verifies what it reads and one named ceiling stands over one directory -- plus the stash_record red closed whole, which pulled in five more guards: log_file_claim, reds_spine_derive, reds_pin_capacity, fold_shelf_link_repoint and shell_dialect_touch. No ceiling raised on a pin, no peer's lane entered, no published number moved
status GREEN -- the full hot roster pass read guards_run=200 guards_green=197 guards_red=0 guards_gated=3 tree_moved=no run_verdict=ok in 1,697s before the commit; individually mantra_store, mantra_declaration_walk, rye_witness_walker, rish_report_bound, mantra_weave_model, mantra_weave_v1_write, mantra_weave_v1_lift, mantra_weave_merge, mantra_diff, rw1_history_contract, stash_record, log_file_claim, log_has_a_row, reds_spine_derive, reds_pin_capacity, reds_ledger_headline, fold_shelf_link_repoint, shell_dialect, shell_dialect_touch, exec_bit, declared_ceiling, tame_style_check and width-check all green on metal; the cold open was spoiled by a peer's pull mid-run and its four stale reds re-run individually; the hot pass is this commit's receipt
recommend keep-going -- the card ran out of room twice in one round and the account had to be cut to a pointer both times, which is the shape four ships have now flagged; and in this lane the store's refusal reaches a user as a Zig stack trace where every other error in the CLI is one plain line, and mantra status and print_usage both print an em-dash in program output that no ASCII guard reads; both are small, both are in this lane, and neither needs a ruling
